'' A STRING ARGUMENT TO A TYPE CONSTRUCTOR IS EVALUATED ONCE. LowerCtorInit lowered every
'' argument for the overload pick and then lowered a string one AGAIN from its node for the
'' parameter it binds, so 'dim as Holder h = Holder( FromNarrow( ) )' called FromNarrow
'' twice and the first result -- a ustring pool temporary -- was never freed. fbsqlite's
'' 'DbValue( hFromUtf8( raw, n ) )' did that per text column: after 256 of them every
'' ustring trim, str and return in ApexWealth came back empty. Measured, fbc calls it once
'' for a byref and a byval parameter alike. The golden holds one call per procedure.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/ctor-string-arg-once.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' GOLDEN: expected/ctor-string-arg-once.out
